 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Of course. How old are they? Then simple sandwiches and fruit are good choices. Pick a spot that' easy to get to without getting hot, and that everyone can see. Cut them into little bits so they don't disappear too quickly. A box of ready made sandwiches is also a time saver. Invite games that build confidence rather than embarrass someone. Musical chairs and tag are good ones. Keep the sun off with a tree shade and plenty of water that doesn't boil the milk in sandwiches. Yes, and a small blanket for cold hands. A towel to dry hands too, if you think the sun might drop.",
